---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Bandarmology" current="bandar"
  description="Who is buying big and who is selling on the IDX's most-traded stocks: big-money pressure, foreign money and churn, from the daily broker summary.">

  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head bm-head">
      <h1>Who's buying big, who's selling</h1>
      <p class="dek">For the most-traded stocks on the IDX: whether the brokers trading in unusually large orders
        leaned to buying or selling, and where foreign money went. This shows what happened, not what happens next.</p>
    </header>
  </div>

  <div class="toolbar">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="toolbar-label" id="band-label">Show</span>
      <div class="segmented" id="band" role="group" aria-labelledby="band-label">
        <button type="button" data-band="all" aria-pressed="true">All <span class="bm-n" data-count="all"></span></button>
        <button type="button" data-band="buy" aria-pressed="false">Big buyers <span class="bm-n" data-count="buy"></span></button>
        <button type="button" data-band="sell" aria-pressed="false">Big sellers <span class="bm-n" data-count="sell"></span></button>
        <button type="button" data-band="weak" aria-pressed="false" title="Big buyers while the price was flat or falling">Buying into weakness <span class="bm-n" data-count="weak"></span></button>
      </div>
      <span class="spacer"></span>
      <input type="search" id="search-input" class="search" placeholder="Find a ticker" aria-label="Find a ticker">
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap bm-split">
    <aside class="bm-list" aria-label="Stocks">
      <div class="bm-list-head" role="group" aria-label="Sort the list">
        <button type="button" data-sort="code">Stock</button>
        <button type="button" data-sort="ret20" title="Price change over the last 20 sessions">Price 20d</button>
        <button type="button" data-sort="lpm20z" aria-pressed="true" title="Did big orders lean to buying or selling over 20 sessions, compared with what is usual for this stock?">Big money</button>
        <button type="button" data-sort="flow20" title="Net foreign buying over 20 sessions, rupiah">Foreign</button>
      </div>
      <ul class="bm-rows" id="bm-rows" role="listbox" aria-label="Stocks" tabindex="0"></ul>
      <p class="bm-empty" id="bm-empty" hidden>No stock matches.</p>
    </aside>

    <section class="bm-detail" id="bm-detail" aria-labelledby="stock-title" tabindex="-1">
      <div class="bm-detail-head">
        <h2 id="stock-title">—</h2>
        <span class="bm-price" id="stock-price"></span>
      </div>
      <p class="bm-read" id="stock-read" aria-live="polite">Loading the broker summaries…</p>
      <dl class="bm-facts" id="stock-facts"></dl>

      <div class="bm-chart">
        <h3>Price</h3>
        <div class="chart"><canvas id="price-chart" class="bm-tall" role="img" aria-label="Price chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="price-tip"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bm-chart">
        <h3>Big-money pressure</h3>
        <p>Rises on days when large orders lean to buying, falls when they lean to selling. What matters is the direction, not the level.</p>
        <div class="chart"><canvas id="lpm-chart" role="img" aria-label="Big-money pressure chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="lpm-tip"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="bm-chart">
        <h3>Foreign money</h3>
        <p>Running total of foreign buying minus selling, in rupiah.</p>
        <div class="chart"><canvas id="flow-chart" role="img" aria-label="Foreign money chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="flow-tip"></div></div>
      </div>

      <details class="bm-more">
        <summary>More readings</summary>
        <div class="bm-chart">
          <h3>Big money, day by day</h3>
          <p>Each session's push. Green, large buyers outweighed large sellers; red, the reverse.</p>
          <div class="chart"><canvas id="lpmday-chart" role="img" aria-label="Daily big-money chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="lpmday-tip"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bm-chart">
          <h3>Churn</h3>
          <p>How many times the shares that actually changed hands were traded back and forth. Near 1, one-way flow; high, brokers trading with each other.</p>
          <div class="chart"><canvas id="vr-chart" role="img" aria-label="Churn chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="vr-tip"></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="bm-chart">
          <h3>Order concentration</h3>
          <p>High when a lot of volume goes through few trades. Only compare a stock with its own past.</p>
          <div class="chart"><canvas id="int-chart" role="img" aria-label="Order concentration chart"></canvas><div class="bc-tip" id="int-tip"></div></div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </section>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="bm-notes" aria-labelledby="notes-title">
      <h2 id="notes-title">How to read this page</h2>

      <div class="bm-notes-grid">
        <div>
          <h3>It is not a buy signal</h3>
          <p>We tested these readings on 170 liquid stocks from 2021 to 2026, buying the session after each reading and
            paying trading costs. Big-money pressure on its own had no reliable edge. Buying into weakness was followed by
            <em>worse</em> returns in 2023–24, and following foreign money only helped in 2021–22. Use the page to see who
            traded how, not to pick what to buy.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h3>What counts as big money</h3>
        <p>A broker counts as big in a stock on a given day when its average order is larger than three quarters of
          that stock's daily average orders over the last 200 sessions. Each day, the line moves by the price times the gap
          between the big buyers' and the big sellers' average order: up when the big buyers' orders are larger, down when
          the sellers' are.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h3>What strong buying and selling mean</h3>
        <p>We take the change in big-money pressure over the last 20 sessions and compare it with how much this stock's
          reading usually moves. About one usual swing up is buying; two or more is strong buying, and selling works the
          same way down. Because each stock is measured against itself, a small cap and BBCA can be compared. A stock needs
          60 sessions of history before it gets a label. Buying into weakness means big buyers while the price was flat or
          down over the same 20 sessions.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
        <h3>Where the numbers come from</h3>
        <p>Stockbit's daily broker summary: every broker's buying and selling in each stock, with lots and number of
          trades. It's updated after the close each weekday for the 100 most-traded stocks by daily value.
          Big-money pressure follows Bandar Metrics' Liquidity Pressure Model (LPM). Bandar Metrics multiplies each stock's
          line by its own fixed number; we leave that out, so the shape matches theirs but the numbers don't.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    .bm-head { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 20px; }
    .bm-n { margin-left: 4px; color: var(--ink-faint); }

    .bm-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(360px, 450px) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0 40px; align-items: start; }

    /* The list stays in view while the charts beside it scroll. */
    .bm-list {
      position: sticky; top: calc(var(--bar-h) + var(--toolbar-h));
      max-height: calc(100vh - var(--bar-h) - var(--toolbar-h));
      display: flex; flex-direction: column;
      border-right: 1px solid var(--rule);
      padding: 16px 16px 16px 0;
    }
    .bm-list-head, .bm-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 50px 66px 1fr 64px; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
    .bm-list-head { padding: 0 10px 8px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); }
    .bm-list-head button {
      border: 0; background: none; padding: 4px 0; cursor: pointer; text-align: right;
      font: 500 .74rem/1.2 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); white-space: nowrap;
    }
    .bm-list-head button:first-child, .bm-list-head button[data-sort='lpm20z'] { text-align: left; }
    .bm-list-head button:hover { color: var(--ink); }
    .bm-list-head button[aria-pressed='true'] { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
    .bm-list-head button[aria-pressed='true']::after { content: ' ▾'; color: var(--gold); }
    .bm-list-head button[aria-pressed='true'][data-dir='asc']::after { content: ' ▴'; }

    .bm-rows { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; overflow-y: auto; overscroll-behavior: contain; scrollbar-width: thin; }
    .bm-rows:focus-visible { outline-offset: -2px; }
    .bm-row {
      padding: 9px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); cursor: pointer;
      font: 500 .84rem/1 var(--mono); font-feature-settings: 'tnum' 1;
    }
    .bm-row:hover { background: rgba(166,122,38,.08); }
    .bm-row[aria-selected='true'] { background: var(--paper-deep); box-shadow: inset 3px 0 0 var(--ink); }
    .bm-code { font-weight: 700; }
    .bm-ret, .bm-flow { text-align: right; }
    .bm-pos { color: var(--up); }
    .bm-neg { color: var(--down); }
    .bm-quiet { color: var(--ink-faint); }

    /* Big money: a bar either side of a centre line, plus the word, so the reading never rests on colour alone. */
    .bm-pressure { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px 1fr; align-items: center; gap: 8px; min-width: 0; }
    .bm-bar { position: relative; height: 8px; background: var(--rule-soft); border-radius: 2px; }
    .bm-bar::before { content: ''; position: absolute; left: 50%; top: -3px; bottom: -3px; width: 1px; background: var(--ink-faint); }
    .bm-bar i { position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; border-radius: 2px; }
    .bm-word { font: 500 .72rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
    .bm-word.strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
    .bm-empty { color: var(--ink-faint); padding: 16px 10px; margin: 0; }

    .bm-detail { padding: 24px 0 40px; min-width: 0; }
    .bm-detail:focus { outline: none; }
    .bm-detail-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .bm-detail-head h2 { margin: 0; font: 600 clamp(2.2rem, 4vw, 3rem)/1 var(--display); letter-spacing: -.02em; }
    .bm-price { font: 500 1rem/1 var(--mono); color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .bm-price b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
    .bm-read { margin: 12px 0 0; max-width: 62ch; font: 400 1.18rem/1.45 var(--text); }
    .bm-facts { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); margin: 20px 0 8px; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
    .bm-facts > div { padding: 12px 16px 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
    .bm-facts dt { font-size: .92rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
    .bm-facts dd { margin: 4px 0 0; font: 600 1.15rem/1.2 var(--mono); font-feature-settings: 'tnum' 1; }

    .bm-chart { margin-top: 28px; }
    .bm-chart h3 { margin: 0; font: 600 1.15rem/1.2 var(--display); }
    .bm-chart p { margin: 4px 0 8px; color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: .98rem; max-width: 70ch; }
    .bm-chart .chart canvas { height: 190px; }
    .bm-chart .chart canvas.bm-tall { height: 320px; }
    .bm-more { margin-top: 32px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: 16px; }
    .bm-more summary { cursor: pointer; font: 600 1.05rem/1.2 var(--display); }
    .bm-more summary:hover { color: var(--gold); }

    .bm-notes { padding: 48px 0 8px; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
    .bm-notes h2 { margin: 0 0 6px; font: 600 clamp(1.4rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem)/1.15 var(--display); letter-spacing: -.01em; }
    .bm-notes-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0 48px; }
    .bm-notes-grid > div { padding: 20px 0 22px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft); }
    .bm-notes h3 { margin: 0 0 6px; font: 600 1.1rem/1.3 var(--display); }
    .bm-notes p { margin: 0; color: var(--ink-soft); line-height: 1.6; }
    .bm-notes em { color: var(--ink); }

    @media (max-width: 960px) {
      .bm-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .bm-list { position: static; max-height: 55vh; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-right: 0; }
      .bm-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
      .bm-notes-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    }
    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .bm-facts { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      /* No room for bar and word: the word carries the reading. */
      .bm-pressure { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .bm-bar { display: none; }
      .bm-chart .chart canvas.bm-tall { height: 260px; }
    }
  </style>
  <script src="../lib/bandarmology.js"></script>
</Base>
